  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Jacket potato with cheese and beans is one of the most reliable British meals: a large floury potato baked at high heat until the skin is properly crisp and the inside is fluffy, then loaded with butter, melted cheddar, and hot baked beans. The skin matters. A potato roasted in foil steams rather than bakes and never gets the crust."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
