        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Bake the potatoes"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the oven to 220°C. Scrub {{potato}} potatoes and pat dry. Rub all over with {{sunflower-oil}} of oil and a generous pinch of salt. Prick several times with a fork."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Place directly on the oven rack or on a baking tray. Bake for 70 to 80 minutes until the skin is crunchy and a knife slides into the centre without any resistance. Large potatoes need the full time."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Heat the beans and serve"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "About 5 minutes before the potatoes are done, heat {{baked-beans}} of baked beans in a small saucepan over medium heat, stirring, until hot through."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Cut each potato across the top with a deep cross. Push the ends to open the potato up. Add {{unsalted-butter}} of butter inside and let it melt. Season with pepper."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Spoon the hot beans over the potato. Scatter {{cheddar}} of grated cheddar on top. Serve straight away while the cheese melts."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "rows": [
            {
              "symptom": "Skin is soft and leathery, not crisp",
              "cause": "Wrapped in foil or oven temperature too low",
              "fix": "Never use foil. Rub the skin with oil and salt, place directly on the rack, and keep the oven at 220°C."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Inside is hard or waxy",
              "cause": "Wrong variety of potato used",
              "fix": "Use a floury potato such as a King Edward or Maris Piper. Waxy varieties stay dense when baked."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Potato not cooked after 80 minutes",
              "cause": "Potato too large or oven temperature inaccurate",
              "fix": "Test with a skewer: it should slide through with no resistance. If not, give it another 15 minutes."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Beans spit and burn",
              "cause": "Heat too high on the hob",
              "fix": "Heat beans over medium-low heat with a lid on for the last minute. Stir regularly."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The baked potato has been on British menus since the nineteenth century, but the loaded jacket potato became a lunchtime staple in the 1970s and 1980s, fuelled by high-street potato stalls and works canteens. Cheese and beans is the most common filling in Britain by a considerable margin. The other standard is tuna mayonnaise, which has its own entry in this library."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}